---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import evidence from '../../../../../public/equipment/14-02/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/14-02/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/14-02/',doc='https://www.instron.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/5960-dual-column-table-frames-system-support.pdf',inst='https://mse.ucr.edu/facilities/instron',fx='https://www.instron.com/en/products/testing-accessories/flexure-fixtures/three-point-bend-test-fixtures/';
const fields=[['widthMm','Width (mm)',2,25,10],['thicknessMm','Thickness (mm)',.5,8,2],['lengthMm','Beam length (mm)',20,200,54],['spanMm','Support span (mm)',0,160,40],['modulusGPa','Reference modulus (GPa)',.1,30,3],['dropMm','Midspan drop (mm)',0,5,.4]];
const show=x=>typeof x==='string'?x:Object.entries(x).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+(typeof v==='number'?Number(v.toPrecision(8)):String(v))).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="Instron 5969 three-point bend" subtitle="" description="Bend an inert beam on two rollers and measure force versus midspan deflection." wide={true}>
<article id="flex-bench" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/14-02/">← Equipment 14-02</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#flex-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">14-02 / Mechanical characterization / Three-point bend</p><h2>Instron 5969</h2><p>Bend a rectangular reference beam on two lower rollers. The example uses a 40 mm span and 0.4 mm drop. Run it, then switch to 80 mm and re-zero to see why span matters so much.</p></header>
<div class="f-grid"><section class="f-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the fixture</h3><div class="f-row" id="flex-views">{['Bench','Front','Side','Fixture'].map(k=><button data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="flex-xr" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div>
<canvas id="flex-model" aria-label="Orbitable Instron 5969 with two lower rollers and central loading nose"></canvas><p id="flex-view-status" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p>Drag to orbit; scroll or pinch to zoom. A lower roller changes the demo span, the nose zeros, and the pendant runs the sweep. Use the buttons for equivalent keyboard actions.</p></section>
<section class="f-card"><h3>02 · Set the span and acquire</h3><form id="flex-form"><div class="f-row"><button type="button" id="flex-span">Toggle 40/80 mm</button><button type="button" id="flex-load">Remove beam</button><button type="button" id="flex-tare">Zero nose</button></div>
<div class="f-fields"><label>Specimen ID<input name="sampleId" required maxlength="96" value="elastic-beam-01"/></label><label>Readout limit<select name="cellN"><option value="500">500 N cell</option><option value="50">Virtual 50 N limit</option></select></label>
{fields.map(([k,t,l,h,v])=><label>{t}<input name={k} type="number" min={l} max={h} step="any" value={v}/></label>)}</div><div class="f-row"><button id="flex-run" type="submit" class="f-run">Run bend test</button><button id="flex-reset" type="button">Restore example</button></div></form><p id="flex-status" role="status">Beam placed and zeroed.</p></section></div>
<section class="f-card"><h3>03 · Force–deflection</h3><p id="flex-result" role="status">No curve acquired.</p><svg id="flex-chart" viewBox="0 0 550 200" role="img" aria-label="Three-point bending force and midspan displacement"></svg><div class="f-row"><button id="flex-json" disabled>Result JSON</button><button id="flex-csv" disabled>Point CSV</button></div></section>
<section><h3>Frame and reference images</h3><div class="f-grid"><figure><img src={a+'front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original dual-column 5969 model projection"/><figcaption>Original enclosure reconstruction. Compare <a href={doc}>M10-16248-EN, Fig. 2-1 and Table 2-5</a>.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original central nose and two independently adjustable lower rollers"/><figcaption>Original simplified three-point fixture. <a href={fx}>Instron standard fixture architecture</a>.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>Selected 5969 standard height and width: 779 × 1,634 × 725 mm W/H/D and 418 mm horizontal test daylight per the manual. <a href={inst}>UC Riverside documents</a> a 5969 with a 500 N static cell and three-point flexure. Housing, accessory offsets and exact roller form are inferred; no certification or specific serial is claimed.</p></section>
<section><h3>Model and export contract</h3><p>Rigid, frictionless lower supports and one central load give Euler–Bernoulli stiffness 48EI/L³, I = bh³/12, maximum stress 3FL/(2bh²), and outer strain 6hδ/L². Fitting uses valid force samples through the zeroed datum. Opening the span changes its cubic effect, not the beam cross-section. The software rejects zero span, a short beam and spans under 16× thickness. Points over 2.5% of span in deflection or 2% outer strain are withheld; an overrange readout withholds force but preserves simulated demand.</p>
<p>Inputs: specimen ID, rectangular width, thickness and length, span, modulus, displacement and selected limit. Output is a specimen-tagged SI force–deflection curve with stress, strain, support IDs, flags and revisions. Only inert elastic flexure is implemented; not tension, compression, plasticity, rate effects or real equipment operation. <a href={a+'output-schema.json'}>Output schema</a> · <a href={a+'example-result.json'}>Example result</a>.</p></section>
<section id="flex-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="f-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{evidence.map(q=><tr><td>{q.id}</td><td>{show(q.expected)}</td><td>{show(q.actual)}</td><td>{q.tolerance??'Exact state'}</td><td>{q.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared analytic fixtures</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Evidence</a> · <a href={a+'instron-5969.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable source</a> · <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>Generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Interaction anchors</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles and {m.draws} material draws. Optional WebXR controller control; no physical headset claim.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/14-02/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#flex-bench header{padding:1.4rem 0;max-width:72ch}#flex-bench h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.25rem 0}#flex-bench section{margin:1rem 0}.f-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.f-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.85rem;min-width:0}.f-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.f-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.f-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.5rem}.f-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.f-fields :is(input,select),#flex-bench button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;border-radius:3px;box-sizing:border-box}.f-fields option{background:var(--menuBg,Canvas);color:var(--text,CanvasText)}#flex-bench button:disabled{opacity:.55}.f-run{background:#3d596f!important;color:white!important}#flex-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;touch-action:none;background:#edeae3}#flex-chart{width:100%;max-height:13rem}.f-scroll{overflow:auto}#flex-bench table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#flex-bench td,#flex-bench th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#flex-bench figure{margin:0}#flex-bench img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.f-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.f-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
</style>
